tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:1: # T-GPLR-58 K-SCALING PROBE (owner-requested 2026-09-23): "increase the slots until
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:2: # predictions actually fit, then measure how many predictions are met."
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:3: #
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:4: # QUESTION: A3 proved the K=2 cache admits ZERO speculative fills (0.00% fill room).
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:5: # The fill-room analyzer (host-only, from the RECORDING of retention legs) says the
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:6: # admittable fraction grows with K (0.00% / 1.85% / 6.62% at K=2/4/8). Nobody has ever
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:7: # run the ARM itself at higher K to see:
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:8: #   1. how many proposals the planner actually PLACES (submitted > 0), and
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:9: #   2. how many of those placed guesses are later CONFIRMED by a demand
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:10: #      (the share(arm) - share(off) delta at the SAME K, and the consumed counter).
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:11: #
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:12: # DESIGN (the control the probe needs): bigger K alone improves retention (the recorded
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:13: # honest ladder: 0.3778 / 0.5355 / 0.6487 / 0.7283 at K=2/4/6/8). So every K gets an
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:14: # OFF TWIN in the same session, and the arm's NET effect is share(arm@K) - share(off@K),
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:15: # never share(arm@K) vs a different-K baseline. The null@K8 controls the placement
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:16: # policy at the ladder's mid point: it proposes the arm's counts structure-free, so any
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:17: # gain it shows is placement/pool growth, not prediction.
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:18: #
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:19: # LEGS (one mutex hold, ~5 min of model time):
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:20: #   off-k4  off-k8  off-k12   retention-only twins at each depth (roles: off)
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:21: #   null-k8            the count-matched structure-free control at K=8
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:22: #   arm-k4  arm-k8  arm-k12   the coact arm at each depth (mode 2, budget 8)
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:23: #
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:24: # VRAM BUDGET (linear from the MEASURED anchors 7.19 GiB peak @K2, 8.37 @K4; +1.07 GiB
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:25: # per K step): K=12 predicts ~16.9 GiB peak vs 22.3 GiB free at session start. The
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:26: # engine's own byte-account preflight refuses loudly if a placement would not fit, so
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:27: # an over-budget leg is a leg FAIL that halts the series, not a silent mis-measurement.
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:28: #
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:29: # DISCIPLINE (the A3 skeleton, kept): the shape is the declared 885-token prompt,
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:30: # --tg-tokens 256, --rep-penalty 1.15 on EVERY leg; share is owned by
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:31: # tools/check-tg-predict.py per leg (never recomputed here); resolved state is read
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:32: # from the trace, not the command line; --check-telemetry gates every leg; the
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:33: # fill-room ceiling is measured per arm leg by tools/analyze-gplr58-fill-room.py; a
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:34: # leg that fails its integrity gates HALTS the series (the remaining legs would measure
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:35: # a broken mechanism); arm-verdict provenance is written for every leg.
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:36: #
tools\run-gplr58-kprobe.ps1:37: # THIS IS A PROBE, NOT A CONTRACT SESSION: it pre-registers NO M-band verdict. The M
